.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH npack 1  "npack 0.2.9"
.SH NAME
npack \- A Nostr\-native package manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBnpack\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
A Nostr\-native package manager
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
npack\-hash(1)
Calculate the SHA\-256 hash of a file
.TP
npack\-verify(1)
Verify a package archive or external manifest
.TP
npack\-install(1)
Install a local .npk or resolve and install a package from Nostr
.TP
npack\-list(1)
List installed packages
.TP
npack\-verify\-installed(1)
Verify the files and metadata of installed packages
.TP
npack\-release\-event(1)
Create a signed Nostr package release event
.TP
npack\-verify\-event(1)
Verify a signed release event against a package manifest
.TP
npack\-revoke\-event(1)
Create a signed revocation event for a package release
.TP
npack\-search(1)
Search Nostr relays for available packages
.TP
npack\-fetch(1)
Download an artifact by its SHA\-256 hash
.TP
npack\-publish(1)
Upload an artifact and publish its package events
.TP
npack\-announce(1)
Publish a signed Nostr text note
.TP
npack\-generate\-key(1)
Generate a new publisher key and register it in the OS credential store
.TP
npack\-register(1)
Register a Nostr secret key in the OS credential store
.TP
npack\-init(1)
Create package metadata for a new project
.TP
npack\-man(1)
Render the complete command reference as a man page
.TP
npack\-install\-ref(1)
Install a package\*(Aqs latest available version, or update all packages
.TP
npack\-pack(1)
Build a deterministic .npk archive from a package directory
.TP
npack\-remove(1)
Remove an installed package
.TP
npack\-inspect(1)
Display metadata embedded in an .npk archive
.TP
npack\-manifest(1)
Extract the embedded manifest from an .npk archive
.TP
npack\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.2.9
